# Mode A vs Mode B Scoring API Constraint

This project has two scoring modes. Getting the API wrong for Mode A silently corrupts experiment data.

## Mode A — Likelihood / NLL scoring
Requires token log-probs over the **input** (prompt echo logprobs), NOT just generated-token logprobs.

**Valid targets only:**
- Small models run locally via `transformers` / `llama.cpp` (SmolLM-360M, Qwen2.5-3B, Phi-4-mini, Gemma3-4B)
- Completion endpoints that explicitly support `echo=True` + `logprobs`

**NEVER suggest** a standard chat completion API (OpenAI chat, Together chat, OpenRouter chat) for Mode A — they expose logprobs on generated tokens only. Doing so produces wrong NLL scores with no error.

## Mode B — Prompted suspiciousness scoring
Needs text generation only. Any hosted instruction-tuned model works (Qwen3.5, Llama 4, GLM-5, etc.).

Source: `docs/claude/memory/compute-constraint.md`
